# Wave 1 — Ambient authority and fail-open (CRITICAL)

1. Remove oo_sandbox_apply() from oo_slist_new.
   File: core/list/list.c:99-102.
   Done: list construction does not install seccomp or stamp
   Landlock. Hostile test: OoSList create, then socket() still
   behaves as before apply; no LINUX_LANDLOCK_SECCOMP status.

2. Cap-gate or unexport oo_sandbox_apply.
   Files: sandbox.h, sandbox_config.c, oodar.h include chain.
   Done: apply requires SysCap or is not on the public ABI.
   Contract test covers it with cap=0.

3. Fail closed when seccomp install fails.
   File: sandbox_config.c:79-87.
   Done: fail_closed_on_kernel_miss is ignored (always closed).
   Return string never says SECCOMP_ENFORCED unless g_capf_on==1.
   Hostile test: force filter fail, assert ok=0.

4. Unexport OS helpers from oodar.h.
   Symbols: ffi_verify_signature, path_under_allowdir,
   path_under_sys_lib, oo_process_policy_getenv,
   oo_child_filter_env. Make them static / internal.
   Done: nm -D / public header has none of them. oo_dlopen still
   verifies signatures after FfiCap. sys_exec child still filters
   env. Hostile test: those symbols are not linkable from a
   consumer TU that only includes oodar.h.

5. Reject negative OoStr.len in HMAC and hash helpers.
   Files: sec/crypto/symmetric/hmac.c, hash.c, sha3.c, seal.c.
   Done: len<0 returns empty / fail-closed, no size_t wrap.
   Hostile test: msg.len=-1 does not crash and does not succeed.

# Wave 2 — Capability model (HIGH)

6. Bind Rule 2 into the HMAC.
   File: sec/cap/cap_attenuate_hmac.c.
   Done: MAC is HMAC(key, parent_hmac || parent_rights ||
   child_rights). Forged parent_rights="ffffffff" fails.
   v1 oo_cap_attenuate returns empty (no subset-free mint).
   Hostile test in tests_challenger_attenuate_v2.c.

7. Make OoPathCap a real directory cap and wire FS.
   File: cap_attenuate_path.c plus fs/os/fs.c, fs_dir.c.
   Done: prefix match requires next char '/' or exact end.
   Child prefix must nest under parent prefix. oo_read_file,
   oo_path_exists, oo_file_size, oo_fs_read_dir check it.
   Hostile tests: /tmp vs /tmpfoo; /tmp then /etc must fail.

8. TimeCap/RandCap use full 64-bit make_cap_tok, no band.
   File: sec/cap/cap_time.c.
   Done: no 0x00FFFFFFFFFFFFFF mask, no 0x5/0x6 high bits.
   Same helper as caps.c. tok==0 redraws or aborts.

9. One zeroize for every cap store.
   Files: caps.c plus cap_alloc.c, cap_ffi.c, cap_time.c.
   Done: atexit wipes alloc/ffi/time/rand as well as the 22
   canonical tokens and g_kernel_hmac_key.

10. Decide CompilerRead vs FfiCap on host dumps.
    File: fs/os/host.c. Decision: host_ast_dump / host_check /
    host_token_dump require CompilerReadCap. host_build keeps
    FfiCap. Mark COMPILER_READ implemented=true in cap_table.json.

# Wave 3 — Memory, actors, net, crypto (HIGH)

11. Return plaintext from pq_aead_open on success.
    File: sec/pqc/pq_sig/pq_aead_open.c:116-128.
    Done: success returns pt; tag fail returns empty; empty-pt
    is distinct from auth fail. Wipe keys on every error path
    in pq_aead_seal.c too.

12. Enforce loopback on UDP send and TCP connect.
    Files: netfloor_udp.c, netfloor_tcp.c.
    Decision: comments win. Reject non-127.0.0.0/8 after
    inet_aton / getaddrinfo. Hostile test: 8.8.8.8 fails closed.

13. Lookup write_int/read_int under the alloc mutex.
    File: core/mem/alloc.c.
    Done: foreign pointer and freed pointer fail closed without
    UAF. Table lookup, not ptr-sizeof arithmetic alone.
    Hostile test: free then write_int in another thread.

14. Close actor/channel destroy vs send TOCTOU.
    Files: actor.c, actor_channel.c, actor_thread.c.
    Done: live is checked only while holding the slot mutex.
    Mutex is not destroyed while a waiter can lock it, or boot
    lock covers destroy. Hostile test: 8 threads send vs destroy.

15. Fix actor_restart spawn-fail (live=0, mutex still init).
    File: actor.c restart fail path.
    Done: no double pthread_mutex_init. Slot is fully recycled
    or stays live with an error return.

