# Wave 6 — Medium physics

24. oo_sandbox_probe_backend uses ll_abi_version(), not #ifdef.

25. Make oo_landlock_mark_applied static. Do not trust a public
    bool as “kernel applied”. Prefer restrict_self errno.

26. FS reads: openat + O_NOFOLLOW on the confined dirfd
    (match the write path). No realpath-then-fopen.

27. Drop LL_FS_EXECUTE from Landlock read bits.

28. oo_random and oo_meta_epoch abort() on getentropy failure.
    Do not return -1 or epoch=-1.

29. Arena checkpoint restores {id, off, gen} or the public
    names stop claiming checkpoint/rollback.

30. Weak-ref: increment weak with CAS while strong>0. Never
    free while weak>0. Use epoch. Cap-gate oo_weak_is_alive.

31. Net slot table: one mutex around boot/alloc/lookup/close.

32. One C example in examples/ that grants AllocCap and allocs.
    Update examples/ANCHOR.oo.

# Wave 7 — Floor / later (do not mix into a Patch)

33. Default-deny seccomp, or stop claiming kernel isolation
    for Thread/Net/FS. This is a Floor.

34. 128-bit tokens or kernel-mediated cap store. 64-bit
    user-space tokens remain residual until then.

35. SIGKILL-safe wipe is not possible in user space. Document
    as residual or move tokens to a memfd sealed by Landlock.

36. Real RASP rollback (not g_ck[8] long-long stack).

37. AES-NI / bitsliced AES. Dudect on GCM is Wave 4; constant-
    time AES is this Floor if S-box timing remains.

38. Governance: replace scripts/*.py with .oo or C. Keep at
    most README.md. Split Makefile if the 256-line law is
    applied to it. hip_kern.hip 529 lines: split or exception.

